      "title": "UUP Adjunct Instructor Salary Schedules",
      "description": "Salary Schedules - Administrative Services Gateway - University at Buffalo Skip to Content (UB) Division of Finance and Administration University at Buffalo (UB) Division of Finance and Administration Administrative Services Gateway Building partnerships through collaboration. Toggle Navigation Menu 8/4/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 10/15/25 Managing Procurement 7/17/25 Managing Money 5/6/25 Travel & Expense 5/19/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 5/15/26 Managing Procurement 4/3/25 Managing Money 7/9/26 Traveling for Business Search Administrative Services > Managing People > Managing Human Resources For My Unit > Managing Staff Positions > Classifying Positions > Salary Schedules Managing People Supervising Planning and Evaluating Employee Performance Managing Human Resources For My Unit Getting Started Managing HR Managing Staff Positions Managing UB Jobs Administrative User Account Develop a Workforce Plan Classifying Positions Create or Update Staff Positions Salary Schedules Learn to Use UB Jobs to Submit Position Descriptions Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Recruitment Toolkit Hiring A Candidate Onboarding New Employees Managing Employee Events Developing Employees Time and Attendance Payroll Health and Safety Managing HR For My Unit — Site Map Related Links 7/9/25 For International Faculty and Staff, Students, Visitors 9/2/26 SIRI If you are working remotely or off-campus, you may need to connect to the UB virtual private network (UBVPN) to access these systems. ePTF Login Line Assignment Login Employee Welcome Login SIRI Login UB Jobs Login Salary Schedules Review the New York State and Research Foundation salary schedules. State Research Foundation Research Foundation (RF) Salary Schedules Research Foundation Salary Schedules The salary schedules for the Research Foundation (RF) are updated annually and can also be found on the RF portal broken down by the position classification. Log in to the RF Portal to View Salary Schedules Get a portal ID and password Research Foundation Salary Guidelines Effective July 1, 2026 N.1 $31,200— $51,674 Office Aide Services Worker I Teacher’s Aide Teacher's Aid - Child Care Center Minimum salary must equate to an hourly rate of $15.00/hr. N.2 $33,006— $57,904 Assistant Teacher Child Care Center Medical Lab Worker Patient Care Aide Radio Announcer Research Lab Worker N.3 $34,435— $63,066 Assistant News Director Assistant Radio Engineer Clerk I Medical Office Assistant Secretary 1 Services Worker II Services Worker II (Driver) Teacher (Preschool/Infant/Toddler) - Child Care Ctr. Teacher (School Age) - Child Care Ctr. Teacher's Assistant N.4 $34,919— $67,362 Console Operator I Medical Laboratory Technician I Patient Care Technician Research Technician I N.5 $36,397— $78,119 Clerk II Lead Teacher (Preschool/Infant/Toddler) Child Care Ctr. Secretary 2 Support Services Specialist N.6 $38,387 — $85,065 Administrative Assistant I Clerical Specialist I Console Operator II Medical Laboratory Technician II Patient Care Specialist Publications Assistant I Research Technician II Sr. Medical Office Assistant Services Worker III Services Worker III (Driver) N.7 $40,989 — $96,261 Administrative Assistant II Clerical Specialist II Console Operator III Perfusion Technologist Programming Specialist Publications Assistant II Radiological Specialist Recruiter (Migrant Outreach) Research Technician III Sr. Patient Care Specialist Sr. Recruiter (Migrant Outreach) N.8 $43,320 — $104,805 Analyst Clinical Research Assistant Console Operator IV Editor I Engineering Design Assistant Graphics Specialist Information Systems Technician Programmer Sr. Administrative Assistant Sr. Clerical Specialist Services Specialist N.9 $16.00/hr (current min hourly rate) — $23.73/hr Data Collector Project Aide Research Aide (Undergrad) N.10 $16.00/hr (current min hourly rate) — $44.12/hr Research Analyst Senior Research Aide (Student) Tutor N.11 $16.00/hr (current min hourly rate) — $141.15/hr Facilities Technician Project Support Specialist Research Support Specialist Senior Research Analyst Trainer N.12 $50,548— $124,129 Clinical Practice Plan Specialist Medical Coder Medical Laboratory Technologist Registered Nurse Sr. Perfusion Technologist Sr. Radiological Specialist E.69 $31,318— $271,337 Camp Counselor Camp Counselor - Student Project Instructional Assistant Research Project Assistant (Graduate Student) These exempt positions are not subject to the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) minimum or the NYS Minimum Salary Threshold for exemptions. E.79 $36,633 — $275,875 Academic Counselor Clinical Nurse Specialist Counselor Data Manager/Statistician Dietician/Nutritionist I Dietician/Nutritionist II Education Specialist Educator Engineer Information Systems Assistant (Project) Medical Therapist News Director Nurse Practitioner Physician's Assistant Principal Counselor Principal Education Specialist Principal Medical Laboratory Technologist Principal Medical Therapist Principal Research Support Specialist Production Director Program Director (Radio) Programmer/Analyst (Project) Radio Engineer Scientific Programmer Social Worker Sr. Counselor Sr. Education Specialist Sr. Medical Lab Technologist Sr. Medical Therapist Sr. Programmer/Analyst (Project) Sr. Research Support Specialist Sr. Scientific Programmer Sr. Social Worker Sr. Trainer Teacher Training Program Coordinator E.89 $36,633 — $275,875 Clinical Investigator* Co-Principal Investigator Creative Artist in Residence Postdoctoral Associate** Principal Investigator Principal Research Scientist Research Scientist Sr. Clinical Investigator* Sr. Postdoctoral Associate** Sr. Research Scientist *This position is not subject to Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) minimum. **The minimum annual salary for this position is $49,000. E.99 $36,633 — $275,875 Agency Administrative Officer Assistant Station Manager Clinical Research Associate I Clinical Research Associate II Medical Practice Plan Administrator Nursing Administrator Principal Medical Practice Plan Administrator Principal Nursing Administrator Project Administrative Officer Project Staff Assistant Project Staff Associate Sr. Medical Practice Plan Administrator Sr. Nursing Administrator Station Manager The Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) requires all exempt employees to be paid a minimum of $35,568 annually and/or $684 weekly regardless of Full Time Equivalent (FTE).  In addition, the NYS Minimum Salary Threshold for Administrative and Executive Employees  is $1161.65 weekly for all areas outside of NYC, Long Island, or Westchester. Those areas are higher. Contact a RF Expert Robert Palmer Director Research Foundation (RF) Human Resources Phone: 716-645-4476 Email: rp9@buffalo.edu State Salary Schedules by Bargaining Unit PBANYS Salary Schedules Mobile Users: Swipe to scroll table PBANYS Salary Schedule Effective April 1, 2025 SG Hiring Rate Perf. Adv Step 1 Perf. Adv Step 2 Perf. Adv Step 3 Perf. Adv Step 4 Perf. Adv Step 5 Job Rate Perf Adv 10 Yr. Long Step 15 Yr. Long Step 20 Yr. Long Step Long Max. 25 Yr. Long Step 1 $35,978 $37,245 $38,512 $39,779 $41,046 $42,313 $43,580 $1,267 $45,471 $47,362 $51,027 $52,919 2 $37,080 $38,415 $39,750 $41,085 $42,420 $43,755 $45,090 $1,335 $47,092 $49,093 $52,864 $54,869 3 $38,615 $40,007 $41,399 $42,791 $44,183 $45,575 $46,967 $1,392 $49,054 $51,142 $55,002 $57,091 4 $40,092 $41,560 $43,028 $44,496 $45,964 $47,432 $48,900 $1,468 $51,096 $53,294 $57,257 $59,450 5 $41,720 $43,264 $44,808 $46,352 $47,896 $49,440 $50,984 $1,544 $53,293 $55,605 $59,684 $61,995 6 $43,601 $45,223 $46,845 $48,467 $50,089 $51,711 $53,333 $1,622 $55,767 $58,200 $62,405 $64,838 7 $45,741 $47,430 $49,119 $50,808 $52,497 $54,186 $55,875 $1,689 $58,405 $60,933 $65,235 $67,762 8 $47,997 $49,752 $51,507 $53,262 $55,017 $56,772 $58,527 $1,755 $61,154 $63,781 $68,182 $70,813 9 $50,352 $52,181 $54,010 $55,839 $57,668 $59,497 $61,326 $1,829 $64,075 $66,824 $71,342 $74,086 10 $52,886 $54,811 $56,7