    "https://www.buffalo.edu/administrative-services/careers-at-ub/ny-helps-program.html": {
      "title": "NY HELPS Program",
      "description": "NY HELPS Program - Administrative Services Gateway - University at Buffalo Skip to Content (UB) Division of Finance and Administration University at Buffalo (UB) Division of Finance and Administration Administrative Services Gateway Building partnerships through collaboration. Toggle Navigation Menu 8/4/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 10/15/25 Managing Procurement 7/17/25 Managing Money 5/6/25 Travel & Expense 5/19/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 5/15/26 Managing Procurement 4/3/25 Managing Money 7/9/26 Traveling for Business Search Administrative Services > Careers at UB > NY HELPS Program Careers at UB NY HELPS Program Notice Of Non-Discrimination Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Labor Condition Applications NY HELPS Program For the duration of the NY HELPS Program, titles may be filled via a non-competitive appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the minimum qualifications of the title for which they apply. On this Page Work for New York State [1:10] Grow Your Career with UB About Your Compensation You are hired at the hire rate for the salary grade assigned to your title. Salaries are non-negotiable. Step increases are given annually. Across-the-board increases would be negotiated by your bargaining unit. 9/8/26 Find the current CSEA salary schedules 9/8/26 Find the current PEF salary schedules 9/8/26 Find the current PBANYS salary schedules 9/8/26 Find the current NYSCOPBA salary schedules How We Support You 8/5/15 We support your well being 6/10/26 We care for your health 7/9/25 We support your family needs We help you plan for retirement How We Help You Advance 9/18/25 Personal growth Skill development Educational support 12/20/22 Job coaching services for your career at UB NYS CS Occupational Search UB Jobs Being a Part of the NYS Workforce Start Your Career with NYS Part 1: Starting Your Career at New York State [2:35] Learn More About Civil Service and NYS Part 2: Navigating the Civil Service Exam Process [2:44] Sign up to learn about future exams Find placement and respond to canvasses using the eligible list management system Understand the Merit System Most state employees are in the classified service resulting in their career mobility options being governed by the Merit System. The merit system includes: Taking examinations Eligible lists and the selection process Leaves of absence Probation Voluntary transfers Reinstatements About the Merit System NY HELPS Titles Specific to UB Business Office Assistant 1, SG-06 Series Find Jobs - Office Assistant 1 How to get there There are no educational or experience requirements. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Sign up and take tests to advance within New York State. Growth titles include Office Assistant 2 series and Administrative Assistant 1. Occupational Information Office Assistant 1 Office Assistant 1 Keyboarding Office Assistant 1 Stores/Mail Office Assistant 2, SG-09 Series Find Jobs - Office Assistant 2 How to get there One year of applicable experience. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Sign up and take tests to advance within New York State. Growth titles include Administrative Assistant 1, Office Assistant 3, Stores and Mail Operations Supervisor. Occupational Information Office Assistant 2 Office Assistant 2 Calculations Office Assistant 2 Keyboarding Office Assistant 2 Stores/Mail Library Clerk 2, SG-09 Find Jobs - Library Clerk 2 How to get there One year of full-time clerical experience in a library setting. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Sign up and take tests to advance within New York State. Growth titles include Library Clerk 3. Occupational Information Library Clerk 2 Administrative Assistant 1, SG-11 Find Jobs - Administrative Assistant 1 How to get there Successful completion of the traineeship program. Two years of experience in administrative support. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Sign up and take tests to advance within New York State. Growth titles include Administrative Assistant 2, Office Assistant 3, Stores and Mail Operations Supervisor. Occupational Information Administrative Assistant 1 Program Aide, SG-13 Find Jobs - Program Aide How to get there Three years of experience performing clerical, keyboarding or paraprofessional work in an office environment. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Sign up and take tests to advance within New York State. Growth titles include Office Assistant 3. Occupational Information Program Aide Facilities Plant Utilities Assistant, SG-09 Find Jobs - Plant Utilities Assistant How to get there Learn about the qualifications for Plant Utilities Assistant . How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Plant Utilities Engineer 1. Occupational Information Plant Utilities Assistant Supervising Janitor, SG-11 Find Jobs - Supervising Janitor How to get there Two years of satisfactory full-time experience in the custodial care or cleaning of buildings, offices or institutional residences. One year of experience must have been at a supervisory level. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Sign up to take tests to advance within New York State. Growth titles include Head Janitor. Occupational Information Supervising Janitor Service and Repair Mechanic Electronics, SG-12 Find Jobs - Service and Repair Mechanic Electronics How to get there Four years of experience with the installation, maintenance and repair of electronic equipment. Occupational Information Service and Repair Mechanic Electronics Plant Utilities Engineer 1, SG-14 Find Jobs - Plant Utilities Engineer 1 How to get there Learn about the qualifications for Plant Utilities Engineer How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Plant Utilities Engineer 2. Occupational Information Plant Utilities Engineer 1 Maintenance Supervisor 1 Motor Equipment, SG-14 Find Jobs - Maintenance Supervisor 1 Motor Equipment How to get there One year of experience supervising staff engaged in the maintenance, overhaul and repair of gasoline and/or diesel-powered motor equipment, including passenger vehicles, construction and heavy equipment, freight and other commercial cargo vehicles, self-propelled off-road equipment and non-self-propelled motor equipment. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Maintenance Supervisor 2 Motor Equipment. Occupational Information Maintenance Supervisor 1 Motor Equipment Maintenance Supervisor 2, SG-17 Find Jobs - Maintenance Supervisor 2 How to get there Two years of first-level supervisory experience in either the maintenance and operation of a physical plant, building construction and/or building renovation and/or repair projects. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Maintenance Supervisor 3. Occupational Information Maintenance Supervisor 2 Maintenance Supervisor 3, SG-19 Find Jobs - Maintenance Supervisor 3 How to get there Two years of second-level supervisory experience in the maintenance and operation of a physical plant, building construction and/or building renovation and/or repair projects. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Maintenance Supervisor 4. Occupational Information Maintenance Supervisor 3 Health Related Dental Hygienist, SG-12 Find Jobs - Dental Hygienist How to get there Possession of a license and current registration to practice dental hygiene in New York State. Occupational Information Dental Hygienist Medical Assistant, SG-08 Find Jobs - Medical Assistant How to get there One year of full-time experience performing clinical and clerical support activities in a health care setting; or completion of a college, university, technical school or vocational school medical assistant program. Occupational Information Medical Assistant Medical Laboratory Technician 1, SG-09 Find Jobs - Medical Laboratory Technician 1 How to get there Learn about the qualifications for Medical Laboratory Technician . How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Medical Laboratory Technician 2. Occupational Information Medical Laboratory Technician 1 Medical Laboratory Technician 2, SG-12 Find Jobs - Medical Laboratory Technician 2 How to get there Learn about the qualifications for Medical Laboratory Technician . Occupational Information Medical Laboratory Technician 2 Licensed Radiological Technologist, SG-14 Find Jobs - Licensed Radiological Technologist How to get there License and current registration to practice radiologic technology in New York State. Occupational Information Licensed Radiological Technologist Registered Nurse 1, SG-18 Find Jobs - Registered Nurse 1 How to get there Possession of a license and current registration as a registered professional nurse in New York State. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Registered Nurse Supervisor. Occupational Information Registered Nurse 1 Laboratory Senior Laboratory Animal Caretaker, SG-08 Find Jobs - Senior Laboratory Animal Caretaker How to get there Learn about the qualifications for Senior Laboratory Animal Caretaker. How to advance One year of full-time service as a laboratory animal caretaker in a research facility including but not limited to hospitals, universities, institutions or laboratories; Or, two years of full-time experience in the handling and care of live vertebrate animals in other than a residential setting. Growth titles include Principal Laboratory Animal Caretaker. Occupational Information Senior Laboratory Animal Caretaker Laboratory Technician, SG-09 Find Jobs - Laboratory Technician How to get there 60 college semester credit hours which includes at least 18 semester credit hours in biology, chemistry, physics, health science or science technology; Or, two years of professional experience in either a laboratory or a clinical setting performing technical laboratory tests and procedures; Or, 30 college semester credit hours including at least 18 semester credit hours in biology, chemistry, physics, health science or science technology and one year of professional experience in either a laboratory or a clinical setting performing technical laboratory tests and procedures. Or, an associate's degree or higher in biology, chemistry, physics, health science or science technology. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Senior Laboratory Technician. Occupational Information Laboratory Technician Principal Laboratory Animal Caretaker, SG-11 Find Jobs - Principal Laboratory Animal Caretaker How to get there Two years of full-time service as a laboratory animal caretaker in a research facility including but not limited to hospitals, universities, institutions or laboratories; Or, two years of full-time experience in the handling and care of live vertebrate animals in other than a residential setting. One year of full-time service as a laboratory animal caretaker in a research facility including but not limited to hospitals, universities, institutions or laboratories. Occupational Information Principal Laboratory Animal Caretaker Senior Laboratory Animal Technician, SG-12 Find Jobs - Senior Laboratory Animal Technician How to get there Completed at least 120 semester credit hours of college coursework which includes at least 18 semester credit hours in either biology, chemistry, physics, health science or science technology and six (6) additional semester credit hours in science, mathematics or computer science; Or, three years of satisfactory experience in either a laboratory or clinical setting performing laboratory tests and procedures; Or, a combination of the above equaling three years. College study will be credited in six-month segments, with 15 semester credit hours equaling six months. Credits must include at least 18 semester credit hours in either biology, chemistry, physics, health science or science technology and six (6) additional semester credit hours in science, mathematics or computer science. Occupational Information Senior Laboratory Technician Security Security Services Assistant 1, SG-06 Find Jobs - Security Services Assistant 1 How to get there Registration as a Security Guard by the NYS DOS. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include Security Services Assistant 2. Occupational Information Security Services Assistant 1 University Police Communications and Security Specialist 1, SG-10 Find Jobs - University Police Communications How to get there One year of full-time experience as a Police or Peace Officer; Or, one year of full-time experience as a dispatcher for a public safety agency including fire departments, emergency medical services or law enforcement; Or, one year of active service and an Honorable Discharge from the United States military, where you served as a dispatcher or military police/security personnel. How to advance Take advantage of training opportunities. Growth titles include University Police Communications & Security Specialist 2. Occupational Information University Police Communications & Security Specialist 1 Site Index About the Division of Finance and Administration 1/21/25 Leadership and Organization 3/17/22 Staff Directory UB Directory Emergency 7/21/26 University Police 4/3/25 Emergency Management Policy, Compliance and Internal Controls 4/4/25 UB Policy Library 9/2/26 Internal Controls 4/3/25 Records Management 4/3/25 Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) Internal Audit EthicsPoint HR For Student Employees 5/20/26 College Work-Study 7/9/25 My Benefits 7/9/25 Taxes for International Students 7/9/25 Time Sheets Employment 9/8/26 Required Annual Trainings 9/21/15 Notice Of Non-Discrimination 3/5/26 Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Information for Suppliers Campus Mail 2/4/26 Campus Mail Services Request Resource Planning 10/1/24 Unit Business Officers (UBOs) and Resource Planners Parking and Transportation 8/24/26 Bus and Shuttle Schedules Print Services 3/24/26 Print Services Ordering System Instructions Traveling for Business 11/11/25 Before and During Your Trip UB Sustainability 7/20/26 Get Involved Related Websites 7/21/26 Emerging Leaders Program Office of the Provost Policies and Guidelines for Faculty and Staff Sponsored Projects Services SUNY SUNY RF University at Buffalo Foundation For Administrative Services Staff 2/20/26 VPFA Communicators Toolkit 6/19/26 Business Services Employee Engagement Hub Log In to Procurement Intranet Website Comments 9/30/24 Can't find something? Send us your feedback about the website. University at Buffalo . All rights reserved.  | Privacy | Accessibility Your Privacy is Important To Us. Buffalo.edu uses cookies to help build a better website experience for our visitors. Learn more in our Privacy Policy . Okay"
    },
    "https://www.buffalo.edu/administrative-services/careers-at-ub/notice-nondiscrimination.html": {
      "title": "Notice Of Non-Discrimination",
      "description": "Notice Of Non-Discrimination - Administrative Services Gateway - University at Buffalo Skip to Content (UB) Division of Finance and Administration University at Buffalo (UB) Division of Finance and Administration Administrative Services Gateway Building partnerships through collaboration. Toggle Navigation Menu 8/4/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 10/15/25 Managing Procurement 7/17/25 Managing Money 5/6/25 Travel & Expense 5/19/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 5/15/26 Managing Procurement 4/3/25 Managing Money 7/9/26 Traveling for Business Search Administrative Services > Careers at UB > Notice Of Non-Discrimination Careers at UB NY HELPS Program Notice Of Non-Discrimination Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Labor Condition Applications Notice Of Non-Discrimination Notice of Non-Discrimination The University at Buffalo is committed to ensuring equal employment, educational opportunity, and equal access to services, programs, and activities without regard to an individual's race, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, gender, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, predisposing genetic characteristics, marital status, familial status, veteran status, military status, domestic violence victim status, reproductive healthcare choices, or criminal conviction status. Employees, students, applicants or other members of the University community (including but not limited to vendors, visitors, and guests) may not be subjected to harassment that is prohibited by law or treated adversely based upon a protected characteristic. The University’s policy is in accordance with federal and state laws and regulations prohibiting discrimination and harassment.  These laws include the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 as Amended by the Equal Employment Opportunity Act of 1972, and the New York State Human Rights Law. These laws prohibit discrimination and harassment, including sexual harassment and sexual violence. Inquiries regarding the application of Title IX and other laws, regulations and policies prohibiting discrimination may be directed to Sharon Nolan-Weiss, Director of the Office of Equity, Diversity and Inclusion and Title VI, Title IX, ADA Coordinator, 406 Capen Hall, Buffalo, New York 14260; Tel. (716) 645-2266; email equity@buffalo.edu .  Inquiries may also be directed to the United States Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights, 400 Maryland Avenue SW, Washington, DC 20202-1100; Tel. 800-421-3481; Email OCR@ed.gov . Contact Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Nolan-Weiss, Sharon Director Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Phone: 716-645-2266 Email: senolan@buffalo.edu Site Index About the Division of Finance and Administration 1/21/25 Leadership and Organization 3/17/22 Staff Directory UB Directory Emergency 7/21/26 University Police 4/3/25 Emergency Management Policy, Compliance and Internal Controls 4/4/25 UB Policy Library 9/2/26 Internal Controls 4/3/25 Records Management 4/3/25 Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) Internal Audit EthicsPoint HR For Student Employees 5/20/26 College Work-Study 7/9/25 My Benefits 7/9/25 Taxes for International Students 7/9/25 Time Sheets Employment 9/8/26 Required Annual Trainings 9/21/15 Notice Of Non-Discrimination 3/5/26 Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Information for Suppliers Campus Mail 2/4/26 Campus Mail Services Request Resource Planning 10/1/24 Unit Business Officers (UBOs) and Resource Planners Parking and Transportation 8/24/26 Bus and Shuttle Schedules Print Services 3/24/26 Print Services Ordering System Instructions Traveling for Business 11/11/25 Before and During Your Trip UB Sustainability 7/20/26 Get Involved Related Websites 7/21/26 Emerging Leaders Program Office of the Provost Policies and Guidelines for Faculty and Staff Sponsored Projects Services SUNY SUNY RF University at Buffalo Foundation For Administrative Services Staff 2/20/26 VPFA Communicators Toolkit 6/19/26 Business Services Employee Engagement Hub Log In to Procurement Intranet Website Comments 9/30/24 Can't find something? Send us your feedback about the website. University at Buffalo . All rights reserved.  | Privacy | Accessibility Your Privacy is Important To Us. Buffalo.edu uses cookies to help build a better website experience for our visitors. Learn more in our Privacy Policy . Okay"
    },
    "https://www.buffalo.edu/administrative-services/careers-at-ub/workplace-regs.html": {
      "title": "Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies",
      "description": "Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies - Administrative Services Gateway - University at Buffalo Skip to Content (UB) Division of Finance and Administration University at Buffalo (UB) Division of Finance and Administration Administrative Services Gateway Building partnerships through collaboration. Toggle Navigation Menu 8/4/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 10/15/25 Managing Procurement 7/17/25 Managing Money 5/6/25 Travel & Expense 5/19/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 5/15/26 Managing Procurement 4/3/25 Managing Money 7/9/26 Traveling for Business Search Administrative Services > Careers at UB > Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Careers at UB NY HELPS Program Notice Of Non-Discrimination Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Labor Condition Applications Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Prospective and current employees can be assured that UB complies with all university, Research Foundation, state and federal workplace and employment policies and regulations. Hiring managers are required to comply accordingly. Non-Discrimination and Equal Employment Opportunities (EEO) Policies Relevant policies regarding non-discriminiation and EEO. SUNY Affirmative Action Statement Equal Opportunity: Access, Employment and Fair Treatment in the State University of New York Reasonable Accommodation Policy UB Discrimination and Harassment Policy Research Foundation Commitment to Equal Employment Opportunity Research Foundation Reaffirmation of EEO Policy and Notice to Applicants or Employees Mandatory Postings Information employers are required, by law, to post and share. Criminal Convictions Records, Article 23-A Corrections Law Human Rights Law (PDF) Notice of Compliance for Disability Benefits (PDF) Notice of Compliance for Worker's Compensation (PDF) NYS Minimum Wage (PDF) Equal Employment Opportunity is the Law Poster (PDF) Time Allowed Employees to Vote OSHA — Job Safety and Health Protection Poster Federal Minimum Wage Your Rights Under the Family and Medical Leave Act Poster Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act (USERRA) Poster Notice of Employee Polygraph Protection Act Employee Rights Under the National Labor Relations Act Notice to All Employees Working on Federal or Federally Financed Construction Projects Notice to Employees Working on Government Contracts Annual Security Reports and Crime Statistics Pay Transparency Non-discrimination Provision Downloads SUNY Continuity of Operations Plan For a State Disaster Emergency Involving a Communicable Disease UB Addendum to the SUNY Continuity of Operations Plan for a State Disaster Emergency Involving a Communicable Disease Download the Unemployment Insurance Poster OSHA Summary of Work-related Injuries and Illnesses Key Workplace Information Other information we want you to know as you consider employment at UB: Clean Indoor Air Act Employment of Minors Ensuring Pay Equity by State Employers UB Policy Library Find a listed policy — by its category or alphabetically, search for a policy title or search the library for keyword(s). Search the UB Policy Library Contact an Expert Our Recruitment staff is knowledgeable and eager to help you with your recruitment-related questions or problems. Reach out to us during our business hours by phone, email or fax. Business Hours Monday Through Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. By Email Recruitment ub-jobs@buffalo.edu Applying for the first time Completing a new application takes on average 45 - 60 minutes. Site Index About the Division of Finance and Administration 1/21/25 Leadership and Organization 3/17/22 Staff Directory UB Directory Emergency 7/21/26 University Police 4/3/25 Emergency Management Policy, Compliance and Internal Controls 4/4/25 UB Policy Library 9/2/26 Internal Controls 4/3/25 Records Management 4/3/25 Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) Internal Audit EthicsPoint HR For Student Employees 5/20/26 College Work-Study 7/9/25 My Benefits 7/9/25 Taxes for International Students 7/9/25 Time Sheets Employment 9/8/26 Required Annual Trainings 9/21/15 Notice Of Non-Discrimination 3/5/26 Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Information for Suppliers Campus Mail 2/4/26 Campus Mail Services Request Resource Planning 10/1/24 Unit Business Officers (UBOs) and Resource Planners Parking and Transportation 8/24/26 Bus and Shuttle Schedules Print Services 3/24/26 Print Services Ordering System Instructions Traveling for Business 11/11/25 Before and During Your Trip UB Sustainability 7/20/26 Get Involved Related Websites 7/21/26 Emerging Leaders Program Office of the Provost Policies and Guidelines for Faculty and Staff Sponsored Projects Services SUNY SUNY RF University at Buffalo Foundation For Administrative Services Staff 2/20/26 VPFA Communicators Toolkit 6/19/26 Business Services Employee Engagement Hub Log In to Procurement Intranet Website Comments 9/30/24 Can't find something? Send us your feedback about the website. University at Buffalo . All rights reserved.  | Privacy | Accessibility Your Privacy is Important To Us. Buffalo.edu uses cookies to help build a better website experience for our visitors. Learn more in our Privacy Policy . Okay"
