    "https://www.buffalo.edu/administrative-services/careers-at-ub/labor-condition-applications.html": {
      "title": "Labor Condition Applications",
      "description": "Labor Condition Applications - Administrative Services Gateway - University at Buffalo Skip to Content (UB) Division of Finance and Administration University at Buffalo (UB) Division of Finance and Administration Administrative Services Gateway Building partnerships through collaboration. Toggle Navigation Menu 8/4/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 10/15/25 Managing Procurement 7/17/25 Managing Money 5/6/25 Travel & Expense 5/19/26 Human Resources 10/13/25 Managing Facilities 5/15/26 Managing Procurement 4/3/25 Managing Money 7/9/26 Traveling for Business Search Administrative Services > Careers at UB > Labor Condition Applications Careers at UB NY HELPS Program Notice Of Non-Discrimination Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Labor Condition Applications Labor Condition Applications A Labor Condition Application (LCA) is a document that is filed with the U.S. Department of Labor, Employment and Training Division incident to an H-1B visa petition. Information in Labor Condition Application From the application document you can find out the following: The number of H-1B non-immigrants seeking to be employed The occupational classification in which they will be employed The wages offered The period of employment The location(s) of employment In accordance with 20 CFR § 655. 734 (a)(1)(i), this is to provide you with notice of such filing and to inform you that: “Complaints alleging misrepresentation of material facts in the labor condition application and/or failure to comply with the terms of the labor condition application may be filed with any office of the Wage and Hour Division of the United States Department of Labor.” Download the Labor Condition Application Updated August 7, 2026 Research Scientist - Posted on 8-7-2026.pdf Questions? Email: immgsvc@buffalo.edu Phone: 716-645-2355 Site Index About the Division of Finance and Administration 1/21/25 Leadership and Organization 3/17/22 Staff Directory UB Directory Emergency 7/21/26 University Police 4/3/25 Emergency Management Policy, Compliance and Internal Controls 4/4/25 UB Policy Library 9/2/26 Internal Controls 4/3/25 Records Management 4/3/25 Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) Internal Audit EthicsPoint HR For Student Employees 5/20/26 College Work-Study 7/9/25 My Benefits 7/9/25 Taxes for International Students 7/9/25 Time Sheets Employment 9/8/26 Required Annual Trainings 9/21/15 Notice Of Non-Discrimination 3/5/26 Employment and Workplace Regulations and Policies Information for Suppliers Campus Mail 2/4/26 Campus Mail Services Request Resource Planning 10/1/24 Unit Business Officers (UBOs) and Resource Planners Parking and Transportation 8/24/26 Bus and Shuttle Schedules Print Services 3/24/26 Print Services Ordering System Instructions Traveling for Business 11/11/25 Before and During Your Trip UB Sustainability 7/20/26 Get Involved Related Websites 7/21/26 Emerging Leaders Program Office of the Provost Policies and Guidelines for Faculty and Staff Sponsored Projects Services SUNY SUNY RF University at Buffalo Foundation For Administrative Services Staff 2/20/26 VPFA Communicators Toolkit 6/19/26 Business Services Employee Engagement Hub Log In to Procurement Intranet Website Comments 9/30/24 Can't find something? Send us your feedback about the website. University at Buffalo . All rights reserved.  | Privacy | Accessibility Your Privacy is Important To Us. Buffalo.edu uses cookies to help build a better website experience for our visitors. Learn more in our Privacy Policy . Okay"
