    "https://careermobilityoffice.cs.ny.gov/cmo/gotit/titleinfo.cfm?jobcode=8750100&nu=21": {
      "title": "Department of Civil Service",
      "description": "Career Mobility Office » GOT-IT » Title Details Your browser does not support iFrames Navigation menu Department of Civil Service Online Services Account Login Apply Online My Examination Applications Eligible Lists (ELMS Online) Job Seekers Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement (HELP) program State Examinations Local Examinations Veterans & Individuals With Disabilities Student Internships StateJobsNY State Employees State Examinations Health Benefits Resources Paid Family Leave Paid Parental Leave Career Mobility Office Retirees Health Benefits Resources Retirement Benefits Working After Retirement HR Professionals State Government Local Government Civil Service Institute About Us Sections Positions Career Ladder Job Duties Minimum Qualifications How to Apply Mobility Options GOT-IT Home > Title Search >\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t\tTitle University Police Communications & Security Spec 1 - Grade 10 Positions in this title can be hired through NY HELPS GOT-IT does not provide information on any job postings or job availability. For information on current \r\n\t\t\t\t\tjob postings, please visit StateJobsNY . You may also visit specific New York State Agency websites for information about an agency and \r\n\t\t\t\t\tits job opportunities. Positions This title exists in SUNY and has approximately \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t179 \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpositions. View A Breakdown Of Positions By County * The number of positions is approximate and represents the number of positions established \r\n\t\t\t\t\t(both filled and vacant); it is not an indication or reference to position type or duration, or intent to be \r\n\t\t\t\t\tfilled. Career Ladder A listing of titles that are most commonly used as steps for upward mobility for this title series. Salary Information for University Police Communications & Security Spec 1 Title Grade Hiring Rate/yr Job Rate/yr University Police Communications & Security Spec 1 10 $49,454 $61,010 University Police Communications & Security Spec 2 12 $55,012 $67,564 All salary grades for trainees titles are Non-Statutory (NS) equated to the salary grade identified. These grade equations apply to the starting salaries in their respective salary schedule for the traineeship levels. This title may exist in more than one negotiating unit. This salary schedule represents the most typical salary for this title. Click here to view additional salary information regarding the various bargaining units. An individual's final salary is determined by the Office of the State Comptroller. This salary schedule does not reflect any Special Salary Treatments Job Duties University Police Communications and Security Specialist 1 provide communications, security, and public safety services within a 24/7 operation in the University Police Department at the campuses of the State University of New York. These positions will require working during various shifts and holidays. Their primary responsibility is to function as a desk officer, including communication activities such as dispatching and using various data bases, online systems, and multiple video sources. University Police Communications and Security Specialist 1 are required to wear uniforms. Where appropriate, they also may perform patrol duties and assist University Police Officers. View the classification standard for this title which illustrates the nature, extent and scope of duties and responsibilities of the classes they describe. Summary of Minimum Qualifications For informational purposes only, click on the examination number(s) listed below to see the current or previous examination(s) that are used to fill this title. 26-409010 31-151010 Please note: qualifications for this position may be subject to change. Job postings on StateJobsNY will contain the most up-to-date qualifications. How to Apply All HELP and NY HELPS open positions are now posted on StateJobsNY .\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIt is now even easier for Jobseekers to find openings and connect with New York State agencies. To narrow your search to NY HELPS jobs, click on \"For the General Public\", then \"Search Vacancies\", and select \"Yes\" on the NY HELPS dropdown to narrow your search to NY HELPS jobs. Directions to apply will be specified on each individual job posting. View Open Positions On StateJobsNY Mobility Options Career mobility is not just limited to the titles in the career ladder.  \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tAdditional movement may be achieved through transfer or other examinations. Transfer Titles for University Police Communications & Security Spec 1 For additional information or clarification of transfer determinations , current State employees should \r\n\t\t\t\t\tcontact the Career Mobility Office at (518) 485-6199 or (800) 553-1322. You can also visit ELMS Online to view established open-competitive, promotion, and transition eligible lists. Contact CMO Useful links Feedback Privacy Policy Disclaimer © 2026 Career Mobility Office , New York State Department of Civil Service Department Of Civil Service About Us Agency Overview Executive Leadership Law, Rules & Regulations Stay Informed Join #TeamCivilService Press Releases Get Help Contact Civil Service Equal Opportunity Policy Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Language Access Information Reasonable Accommodation Resources Public Information Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) Eligible Lists (ELMS Online) Open Meetings Test Guides & Resource Booklets Vendor Information DPM-100 Master Equal Employment Opportunity Data Collection Form Online Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Policy CONNECT WITH US FACEBOOK INSTAGRAM LINKEDIN YOUTUBE TWITTER REGISTER TO VOTE Sign up online or download and mail in your application REGISTER NOW Your browser does not support iFrames"
    },
    "http://www.buffalo.edu/provost/universitypolicies.html": {
      "title": "Your Privacy is Important To Us.",
      "description": "University Policies & Guidelines for Faculty & Staff - Office of the Provost - University at Buffalo Skip to Content Your Privacy is Important To Us. Buffalo.edu uses cookies to help build a better website experience for our visitors. Learn more in our Privacy Policy . Okay University at Buffalo (UB) The State University of New York University at Buffalo (UB) Office of the Provost Contact Us About the Provost University Policies & Guidelines for Faculty & Staff Toggle Navigation Menu 8/19/26 Initiatives 8/19/26 Communications 8/19/26 Academic & Administrative Units 8/19/26 Resources 8/19/26 Initiatives 7/8/26 Communications 8/19/26 Academic & Administrative Units 8/19/26 Resources 8/19/26 HWI test site Search Contact Us About the Provost University Policies & Guidelines for Faculty & Staff Office of the Provost > Resources > University Policies & Guidelines for Faculty & Staff Resources University Policies & Guidelines for Faculty & Staff SUNY International Risk Information and Screening Kit (IRISK) Federal Updates and UB Resources Accreditation: Middle States Commission on Higher Education President’s Advisory Council on Race Implementation Resources University Policies & Guidelines for Faculty & Staff This content reflects the subject matter formerly housed in the Faculty Staff Handbook What follows is an index to the subject matter formerly compiled in the faculty staff handbook. All material has been reviewed and approved by the Faculty Staff Handbook Committee and approved by Provost Charles F. Zukoski on March 12, 2018. Note, to search this page use Control+F (PC) or Command+F (Mac). 8/21/26 General Information 8/21/26 Academic Policies 8/21/26 Equity, Diversity and Inclusion 8/21/26 Faculty and Professional Staff Governance 8/21/26 UB Personnel Policies 8/21/26 State University of New York General Information 8/21/26 University Resources and Offices General Information General Information: Office of the President UB's Mission, Vision & Goals University at Buffalo Organizational Chart University at Buffalo Council University at Buffalo Foundation University Police Official Academic Calendar (Office of the Registrar) Holidays (Administrative Services Gateway) Adverse Weather Operations Policy (University Policy Library) From the University Policy Library : Campus Smoke-free Policy Alcohol, Drugs & Narcotics Policy From the Student Life Gateway : Drug Free Schools & Community Act Regarding Information Technology & Network Access: Computer & Network Use Information Security & Data Access UB Network Connection Policy Academic Policies Policies, Procedures & Criteria for Faculty Personnel Actions (including, appointment, reappointment, promotion, and tenure) Teaching & Student Related Matters: Policies from the Undergraduate Catalog : Academic Integrity Academic Standards (Good Standing, Warning, Probation & Dismissal) Faculty Teaching Responsibilities: Course Expectations Course Syllabi Grading Grievance Procedures Notice of Non-discrimination Obstruction or Disruption in the Classroom For additional policy guidance on classroom, course, undergraduate student, and teaching related matters, see the Undergraduate Catalog Policy Library and the Office for Undergraduate Education . Policies from the Graduate School : Academic Integrity Academic Standing Grading Grievance Policies International Teaching, Research, & Graduate Assistants Graduate School Charter and Bylaws For guidance on the policies listed above and for additional classroom, course, graduate student, and teaching related matters, including degree candidacy, residency requirements, TOEFL etc., see the Graduate School Policy Library . Additional University Policy Statements and Guidance: Allowable Use of Funds (from the University Policy Library ) Complaints Against Faculty (from the original Faculty Staff Handbook): Students are advised to see Grievance Policies and Procedures as linked to above in their respective Undergraduate and Graduate guidelines. Disclosure of All Funds Generated Throught the Use of University Faculty/Staff Time or of University Facilities (from the University Policy Library ) Disclosure of Financial Interest (Conflict of Interest) (from the University Policy Library ) Ethics Policy (from the University Policy Library ) See also: NYS Ethics (Conflicts of interest, confidentiality, appearance of impropriety, financial disclosure, moonlighting etc.) Faculty Code of Conduct Faculty Mentoring Policy Mentoring website Mentoring Forms Faculty Responsibility: Policy and Process (pdf) Faculty Voting Eligibility Gifts, Prizes, and Awards Policy (from the University Policy Library ) President's Statement on Political Fundraising (pdf) Responsible Conduct in Research, Intellectual & Creative Activities (from the University Policy Library ) Teaching, Assessment & Improvement Policy (pdf) Tenure Clock Stops Faculty & Professional Staff Governance Policies from the Faculty Senate : Bylaws of the Voting Faculty Charter of the Faculty Senate Standing Orders of the Faculty Senate Statements on Freedom of Expression Policies from the Professional Staff Senate and Governing Documents : Bylaws (pdf) Code of Ethics for Professional Staff (pdf) Constitution (pdf) UB Personnel Policies from the Human Resources & Administrative Gateway Benefits: Accrual Rates (Holiday calendar, vacation & sick time for students, classified, professional and faculty employees from the Administrative Services Gateway) CSEA (Classified Staff) UUP (Faculty) Compensation Leaves of Absence (In cases where leave without pay may be needed, the critical element for granting such leave is the certification by the appropriate officials. Please see your HR administrator for assistance. In computing consecutive years of service for sabbatical leave eligibility, leaves without pay and leaves at partial pay \"shall not be included and shall not be deemed an interruption of otherwise consecutive service\" per the Policies of SUNY's Board of Trustees regarding \"service credits.\") Nepotism Policy For additional information from Human Resources see the Administrative Gateway or the University Policy Library . Approval Authority Policy (Signatory Authority) From the Office for Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Obtaining Assistance Policies: Discrimination and Harassment Policy Recruitment Recruitment Exception Policy Religious Accommodation & Expression ( Statement from the Provost ) Reasonable Accommodation Policy (See also: Accessibility Resources from the Student Life Gateway ) From the Office of the Vice Provost for Inclusive Excellence About Us How We Are Different Strategic Initiatives State University of New York Policies and Guidelines Academic Freedom (Article XI, Title I, SUNY Board of Trustees Policies & Procedures below) Adjudicating Allegations of Unprofessional Conduct (See Faculty Senate Governance Handbook , III.H. and Appendix 4) (pdf) Collective Bargaining Units Disclosure Requirements (State and Federal) Ethics (Conflicts of interest, confidentiality, appearance of impropriety, financial disclosure, moonlighting etc.) Government Relations (State and Federal) Lobbying Law Requirements Political Activity at SUNY Campuses Public Officers Law (Code of Ethics)(pdf) Policies and Procedures of the Board of Trustees Shared Governance Statement of Professional Rights and Responsibilities  (See Faculty Senate Governance Handbook Appendix 4) State Regulations Regarding Business & Professional Activities SUNY-wide Policies & Procedures (Search Engine) Additional University at Buffalo Resources & Offices Administrative Gateway Employee Assistance Program Employee Relations Curriculum, Assessment and Teaching Transformation Office of International Student & Scholar Services Office of the Vice President for Research & Economic Development Forms & Policies Office of the Senior Vice Provost for Faculty Affairs United University Professions Contract & Benefits (2022-2026) University Policy Library University at Buffalo . All rights reserved.  | Privacy | Accessibility"
    }
